  - name: "S.D.C. Mortal"
    description: "No natural A.R. and no M.D.C. - an Ogre needs M.D.C. body armor, a force field or magic. Most prefer heavy armor, up to full environmental and power armor, and adore magic armor and weapons."
restrictions:
  - "Ogres take readily to M.D.C. armor, energy weapons and rail guns, cybernetic implants and partial bionic reconstruction; what stops many from getting bionics is not trusting whoever would do the surgery."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 102-103 (file p103-p104). The Rifts conversion of the Palladium Fantasy Ogre, which is the `ogre` row. A separate class because a variant cannot cross systems.
  - FOUR OF THE ATTRIBUTE DICE DIFFER from the Palladium Fantasy row, read from the page rather than carried over: P.S. 4D6+2 (Palladium 4D6+4), P.E. 4D6 (3D6+6), P.B. 2D6+2 (2D6), Spd 3D6+2 (3D6). The S.D.C. is 40 (Palladium 20), a POOL BONUS.
  - PSIONICS DIFFER TOO: this page says "Standard, about the same as humans", where the Palladium row states none and carries psionics_allowed: false. So this row has no psionics block and no psionics_allowed line.
